DOAS(1)                     User Commands

NAME
    doas - run a command as another account

SYNOPSIS
    doas [-ns] [-C config] [-u name] command [argument ...]
    doas -C config [-u name] [command [argument ...]]

DESCRIPTION
    doas is OpenDoas 6.8.2, compiled unmodified from third_party/opendoas
    against the shadow passwords of minios. It runs command as the account
    name, root by default, when a rule of /etc/doas.conf permits it, and
    asks for the password of the caller unless the rule says nopass. The
    password is read from the terminal without echo, and input typed
    before the prompt appears is discarded. doas is set user id root.

    The command runs with a fresh environment that retains DISPLAY, TERM and
    PATH, sets HOME, LOGNAME, USER and SHELL for the target account and
    DOAS_USER to the name of the caller, and takes the variables named by
    the keepenv and setenv options of the rule. Every permitted command and every refusal is recorded in
    /var/log/messages through syslog(3).

OPTIONS
    -C config   Parse config instead of running a command and report
                syntax errors. With a command, print permit, permit nopass
                or deny for the rule that would apply.
    -n          Fail instead of asking for a password.
    -s          Run the shell of the target account, or the one named by
                SHELL.
    -u name     Run the command as name.

    The -L option and the persist rule option of OpenDoas need a time
    stamp facility that minios does not provide. doas therefore asks for
    the password every time a rule without nopass applies.

FILES
    /etc/doas.conf      the rules, see doas.conf(5)
    /var/log/messages   the log of permitted and refused commands

EXAMPLES
    doas pkg install gedit
    doas -u anna ls /home/anna
    doas -C /etc/doas.conf

SEE ALSO
    doas.conf(5), sudo(1), su(1), id(1), index(7)
